{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>His land is blessed by HaShem.</b> Perhaps because they were destined to say to Joshua, the children of Joseph, that the place was too narrow for them to be a numerous people (Joshua 17:14), therefore he blessed their land to expand. Further, because Joseph sustained and provided for all Israel, and we find that HaShem accounted him for this as though he had begotten them, as it is written (Psalms 77:16): ״בְּנֵי יַעֲקֹב וְיוֹסֵף סֶלָה״, and they said, of blessed memory (Sanhedrin 19b), that because he provided for them they were called by his name — therefore he blessed him with the abundance of the good of the land, measure for measure."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:22:09.283313099Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}